Description: Wild OS Capture: screenshots, screen recording and scanning
 Print Screen and Win+Shift+S bring up the Capture toolbar over a frozen
 screen: take a screenshot or record, of an area, a window, the full
 screen or a freeform shape, now or after a delay. Win+Shift+R starts it
 ready to record.
 .
 Every screenshot goes to the clipboard and opens in the editor, with a
 pen, highlighter, arrow, box, text, blur and crop in five colours. It
 saves to Pictures/Screenshots; recordings go to Videos/Screen recordings.
 KWin takes the pictures and PipeWire carries the recordings.
 .
 The Scan tab scans paper from a network scanner (eSCL and WSD, through
 sane-airscan) or a USB one (SANE), from the glass or the feeder, and
 saves the pages as a PDF or as pictures, or opens them in PDF to sign.
